 "drivingQuestion": "From where do we derive that an acute mourner disqualifies the service?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "Derived by inference from Leviticus 21:12.",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "zevachim.16a.14",
   "daf": "16a",
   "sentenceId": 13,
   "he": "אוֹנֵן מְנָלַן? דִּכְתִיב: ״וּמִן הַמִּקְדָּשׁ לֹא יֵצֵא, וְלֹא יְחַלֵּל״ – הָא אַחֵר שֶׁלֹּא יָצָא, חִילֵּל.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches that rites performed by «an acute mourner» are disqualified. The Gemara asks: «From where do we» derive this? «As it is written» with regard to a High Priest who is an acute mourner: «“And he shall not leave the Sanctuary, and he will not profane» the Sanctuary of his God” (Leviticus 21:12). One can infer: «But» any «other» ordinary priest «who did not leave» the Sanctuary while he was an acute mourner and continued to perform the service «has desecrated» the rites he performed."
  }
 ],
